# Q1: How would a human perform this motion? (One sentence)
# Q1: A human would have a quick, sharp intake of breath, often accompanied by a slight backward jerk of the head and upper body, while simultaneously bringing a hand up to cover their open mouth.
# Q2: Pose Candidates Comparison. Rank at least 2 pose configurations (torso_height, arm_position, gripper_orientation, head, left_arm, x/y/z) and state the winner and why—do NOT pick presets from gesture names alone.
# Q2: Candidate A (Start): Neutral stance with `torso_height: "mid"`, `arm_position: "still"`, `head: "center"`. Candidate B (End): A shocked pose with `torso_height: "low"`, `arm_position: "in"` and `gripper_orientation: "horizontal"` to cover the mouth, and `head: "up"`. Winner: Candidate A for the start; the end state will be achieved via a multi-step sequence for better expression, not a single target pose.
# Q3: Structure Comparison. Compare 2+ full primitive sequences (e.g., M1: pose > movement > pose vs M2: pose > path > path). State the winner and why—**prioritize movement/path beats that express the cue**, not pose-only tweaks.
